{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q906969","formula":"GaO₄P","hill":"GaO4P","elements":["O","P","Ga"],"composition":{"O":4.0,"P":1.0,"Ga":1.0},"names":{"en":"Gallium phosphate","ru":"Фосфат галлия"},"descriptions":{"en":"Gallium phosphate (GaPO4 or gallium orthophosphate) is a colorless trigonal crystal with a hardness of 5.5 on the Mohs scale. GaPO4 is isotypic with quartz, possessing very similar properties, but the silicon atoms are alternately substituted with gallium and phosphorus, thereby doubling the piezoelectric effect. GaPO4 has many advantages over quartz for technical applications, like a higher electromechanical coupling coefficient in resonators, due to this doubling.","ru":"Фосфат галлия — неорганическое соединение, соль галлия и фосфорной кислоты с формулой GaPO4, бесцветные кристаллы, не растворяется в воде, образует кристаллогидраты."},"fame":6,"pubchemCid":9815301,"mass":164.69,"charge":0,"smiles":"[O-]P(=O)([O-])[O-].[Ga+3]","inchikey":"LWFNJDOYCSNXDO-UHFFFAOYSA-K","iupac":"gallium phosphate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-4122","atoms":23,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[4.896,0.0,0.0],[-2.448,4.24,0.0],[0.0,0.0,11.09]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":1.333,"y":2.31,"z":5.545,"el":"Ga"},{"x":-1.115,"y":1.931,"z":1.848,"el":"Ga"},{"x":3.782,"y":1.931,"z":1.848,"el":"Ga"},{"x":2.229,"y":0.0,"z":9.241,"el":"Ga"},{"x":-0.219,"y":4.24,"z":9.241,"el":"Ga"},{"x":1.335,"y":2.312,"z":0.0,"el":"P"},{"x":1.335,"y":2.312,"z":11.09,"el":"P"},{"x":-1.114,"y":1.929,"z":7.393,"el":"P"},{"x":3.783,"y":1.929,"z":7.393,"el":"P"},{"x":2.227,"y":0.0,"z":3.697,"el":"P"},{"x":-0.221,"y":4.24,"z":3.697,"el":"P"},{"x":0.345,"y":1.729,"z":6.974,"el":"O"},{"x":0.779,"y":3.675,"z":10.671,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.124,"y":3.078,"z":3.278,"el":"O"},{"x":2.793,"y":2.512,"z":0.419,"